    "result_text": "No dangling references. The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, rejecting with 409 only on a whole-key match.\n\n**New / changed pieces, each with a single responsibility:**\n\n- **`util/OwnerIdentityKey`** (new) \u2014 the one place that derives an owner's identity key from its already-normalized telephone, email and household id. Reused by both the service and the mapper.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`** \u2014 replaced the three separate telephone/email/household rejections with one `rejectIdentityCollision(owner)` helper. It fetches only the candidates sharing the telephone (a prerequisite for a full-key match) and rejects when any has an equal whole key. Household *grouping* (joining/`householdId` assignment via `sharesHousehold`) is preserved unchanged \u2014 only the duplicate *rejection* moved to the key.\n- **`service/DuplicateOwnerException`** (new) replaces the three removed `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception` classes; **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** now has one 409 handler instead of three.\n- **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 replaced the now-redundant `existsByTelephone`/`existsByEmailIgnoreCase` with a single `findByTelephone` returning the candidate owners, implemented across the Spring Data, JPA and JDBC variants.\n- **`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema and mapped it via `OwnerIdentityKey.of(owner)`, so it's returned in responses.\n\nBecause the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones now derive different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a conflict. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
